## Why the code is vendored

sglang-omni drives the CosyVoice3 TTS pipeline through its own stages (see the
hand-written glue in the package root: `stages.py`, `model_runner.py`,
`request_builders.py`, etc.). The model / flow (DiT CFM) / HiFT-vocoder / frontend /
tokenizer code is vendored so the package is self-contained and does not depend on an
external CosyVoice install.

The autoregressive speech LM is **not** vendored — it is reimplemented natively in
`sglang_model.py` to run on the sglang engine.

## What was pruned from upstream

To keep only the inference path actually exercised by sglang-omni, large parts of the
upstream trees were not vendored. Only the modules reachable from the frontend import
and the sliced flow/HiFT instantiation graph are included; the entire training, CLI,
serving, dataset, and evaluation scaffolding is left out. Notable removals include:

- CosyVoice cli orchestration — `cosyvoice/cli/model.py` and `cosyvoice/cli/cosyvoice.py`
  (the pipeline is driven by sglang-omni stages, not the CosyVoice cli).
- Training / serving / data scaffolding — `cosyvoice/bin/*`, `cosyvoice/dataset/*`, and
  training-only code such as `cosyvoice/transformer/label_smoothing_loss.py`.
- The non-DiT (CosyVoice1/2) flow path — `cosyvoice/flow/decoder.py`,
  `cosyvoice/flow/length_regulator.py`, `cosyvoice/transformer/decoder.py`,
  `cosyvoice/transformer/decoder_layer.py`, `cosyvoice/transformer/encoder.py`.
- The HiFi-GAN training discriminator (only the generator is vendored).
- The dead vendored LM — `cosyvoice/llm/llm.py` (replaced by the native
  `sglang_model.py`).
- From Matcha-TTS, only `BASECFM` (flow_matching.py), `mel_spectrogram` (utils/audio.py),
  and the pylogger are vendored; the Decoder/Transformer components and the rest of the
  package are not.

This list is representative, not exhaustive.

## What was modified locally

Additionally, every vendored file had its intra-package imports rewritten from
`from cosyvoice…` / `from matcha…` to the full
`sglang_omni.models.cosyvoice3.cosyvoice…` / `sglang_omni.models.cosyvoice3.matcha…`
path — a mechanical, non-semantic change applied uniformly across the tree and so
not individually annotated.

All other local divergence from upstream is also marked in-file with a
`# LOCAL MODIFICATION (sglang-omni): …` comment:

- `cosyvoice/cli/frontend.py` — `CosyVoiceFrontEnd.__init__` accepts an explicit
  `device` (from sglang-omni stage placement) instead of always taking the default
  CUDA device, and pins the ORT CUDA provider to that device id.
- `cosyvoice/utils/class_utils.py` — removed the `get_model_type()` helper (it
  dispatched to `cosyvoice.cli.model`, which is not vendored); only the
  `COSYVOICE_*_CLASSES` registries are kept.
- `cosyvoice/utils/file_utils.py` — removed the import-time
  `logging.basicConfig(level=DEBUG)` call (a vendored module must not reconfigure the
  process-wide root logger).
- `cosyvoice/utils/onnx.py` — disabled the import-time ONNX `EmbeddingExtractor`
  (upstream eagerly read a generic `onnx_path` env var and built an online
  speaker-embedding extractor); the sglang-omni pipeline supplies speech tokens and
  the campplus x-vector via the frontend, so `onnx_path` is pinned to `None` and
  nothing is constructed at import.
- `matcha/utils/pylogger.py` — rewritten without the `lightning` dependency.
- `matcha/models/components/flow_matching.py` — kept only `BASECFM`; removed upstream's
  `CFM(BASECFM)` subclass and its `matcha.models.components.decoder` import (CosyVoice3
  uses its own DiT CFM), so the Matcha `decoder.py` / `transformer.py` modules are unused
  and not vendored.

The vendored `matcha/` package `__init__.py` files are kept empty (namespace markers only);
they are not annotated individually. `matcha/utils/audio.py` is vendored as upstream (no local
change) — the pipeline uses only its `mel_spectrogram`.
